WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:05.840
An earthquake has shaken the Spanish island
of La Palma - the strongest tremor since a

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.440
volcano started erupting there last month.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:14.900
No significant damage was reported, but scientists
say it's another sign that the eruption won't

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.240
end soon.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.200
Already it's forced hundreds of residents
to abandon their homes.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:25.380
But the natural spectacle is also attracting
tourists.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.820
Captivated by nature's fury.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:34.410
A fountain of magma gushing from the depths
of the Earth.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:39.890
For almost six weeks, rivers of molten rock
have been flowing from Cumbre Vieja.

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:45.479
Lava, burning at a sizzling 1,300 degrees
Celsius.

00:00:45.479 --> 00:00:51.519
The apocalyptic scene has become an unlikely
tourist attraction.

00:00:51.519 --> 00:00:56.649
The local volcano emergency committee is offering
free shuttles for the catastrophe curious.

00:00:56.649 --> 00:01:05.570
"You hear it and it`s like the world is coming
to an end, it`s impressive."

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:09.490
But many have also come to show their support
for the islanders.

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:16.190
Thousands have had to abandon their homes,
destroyed by the mighty volcano.

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:20.930
"We definitely want to contribute to La Palma’s
economy."

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:25.630
"That's why we came here"
"In a passive way, our way to help is come

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:30.320
here to visit the volcano, which is something
unique, but we contribute with money by spending

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:38.250
money at hotel, restaurants, car rental."

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:43.750
The eruption has hit local businesses hard,
as ash falls like rain, painting the usually

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:50.710
sunny island every shade of gray
Some areas - like here in Las Manchas - more

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:54.900
reminiscent of a lunar landscape:
"The ash cover is very thick.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:02:04.220
The football, the soccer pitch down there
is, well, half up the goal posts covered with

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:13.200
ash and this will take many weeks and months
before this is cleaned up."

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:18.240
Experts say the latest earthquake could be
a sign it's far from over.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:23.290
Ironically, not necessarily bad news for La
Palma's economy.

